; Baselines (doc/manual/baselines.md): both storages, both acceptance
; gestures, and the inline form.
;
; The (test) stanza holds an expect literal in the test file and an
; expect_file against help.expected. It runs the suite with --corrected
; and diffs each corrected file, so a stale expectation shows as a diff
; under `dune runtest` and `dune promote` accepts it — the same
; promotion protocol as for [%expect] and cram tests.
;
; The (library) beside it is the inline form: (inline_tests) with
; (pps ppx_windtrap). dune builds and drives the runner; a stale
; [%expect] payload shows as a diff and is accepted with dune promote.

(test
 (name test_mytool)
 (modules test_mytool mytool)
 (libraries windtrap)
 (deps help.expected)
 (action
  (progn
   (run %{test} --corrected)
   (diff? test_mytool.ml test_mytool.ml.corrected)
   (diff? help.expected help.expected.corrected))))

(library
 (name windtrap_example_expect)
 (modules parser sanitized)
 (inline_tests)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap)))
